:"3-Ga","Cell_line":"MDA-MB-231","Time(h)":25,"IC50_Light(M*10^-6)":"6.382 ± 0.313","IC50_Light_value":6.382,"Excitation_Wavelength(nm)":"625 ± 2","Irradiation_Time(minutes)":60,"Irradiation_Power(W*m^-2)":3000,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1021/acs.jmedchem.4c00249","Year":2024,"Type":"IC50"}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"3-Ga","value":1.24,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"PBS","pH":7.4,"temperature_C":25,"doi":"10.1021/acs.jmedchem.4c00249","year":2024,"record_id":"MLDB-002744","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The shake flask method was applied to measure the lipophilicity of 5FU-gallium corrole conjugates with a UV–vis spectrometer. First, the corrole complexes at different concentrations were prepared in 1-octanol presaturated with PBS (10×, pH 7.4). Then, equal volumes of the PBS presaturated with 1-octanol were added and mixed. The resulting solution was placed in a homoiothermic (25 °C) shaker at 200 rpm for 4 h. After the oil and water distribution achieved equilibrium, the concentration of corrole complexes in the oil layer was obtained by analyzing UV–vis absorption spectra. The octanol/water partition coefficient log PO/W (Po/w = Co/Cw = Ao/Aw, where A represents absorbance) of 5FU-gallium corrole conjugates was calculated by eq 1: (67-69) log𝑃o/w=log{(𝐶o)final/[(𝐶o)initial-(𝐶o)final]}"}]}